# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Sarath Kumar Menon et al. (2024). From electrons to phase diagrams with machine learning potentials using pyiron based automated workflows.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-024-01441-0
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 b7cf99abda7b9fd4...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 672 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/menon2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the HDNNP (RuNNer) and ACE (pacemaker) potentials for
# the Al-Li system trained on the pyiron-generated PBE data set, with
# energy and force RMSE/MAE on their training data and on a common test
# set (Table 1). The EAM potential fitted in the same workflow is
# classical and not encoded. Elastic constants, phase diagrams and
# free energies are property results.

